---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="mdbase Connect"
  description="Choose which apps can use a local folder or hosted mdbase collection, review exact permissions, and revoke access at any time."
  current="connect"
>
  <section class="content-section">
    <h1>Connect</h1>
    <p>
      mdbase Connect allows an application to work with one local or hosted
      collection. The application describes the kinds of records it understands
      and the operations it needs. You choose the collection and review the
      request before access is granted.
    </p>
    <p>
      A grant belongs to a particular application and collection. It might
      allow the application to view, find, create, and edit records while
      leaving deletion unavailable. The authority responsible for the
      collection checks that grant whenever an operation is performed.
    </p>
    <p>
      For a local collection, an open-source connector runs on your computer
      and performs approved operations against the folder. The Connect control
      plane coordinates authorization and routing but does not receive the
      operation payloads or results.
    </p>
    <p>
      For a hosted collection, the provider keeps the authoritative copy online
      and performs the same operations there. A local Markdown mirror can be
      retained for offline work.
    </p>
    <p>
      Access can be narrowed, paused, or revoked later. This changes what the
      application may do; it does not alter ownership of the collection or
      prevent other tools from using it.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/beta/">Join the open beta</a> or
      <a href="https://connect.mdbase.dev/login">sign in</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Trust boundary</h2>
    <p>
      Connect does not make every component equally trusted. A local connector
      can read the local folder. A hosted provider can decrypt hosted records in
      order to process them. Applications receive only the operations in their
      active grants. The control plane can identify accounts, applications,
      collections, and grants, but cannot read local collection contents.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <a href="/security/">security documentation</a> describes these
      boundaries and their limitations in detail. Developers can continue with
      the <a href="/sdk/connect-quickstart/">Connect application guide</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
